d of things that seem even more  extreme than than we would have imagined  or the public would have imagined it was  it was a really uh  surprising conversation so one thing  that's revealed is that this employee  kept a file he was told to delete 180  hours of audio recordings where is that  content now and what's happened to it so  we've reviewed a copy of the audio  recording in order to authenticate that  it was real and it was really disturbing  to listen to you know britney is being  recorded in her bedroom and her  interactions and conversations with her  kids her boyfriend and others were  secretly recorded  so matthew just told me he's uh he's  going to keep looking into this he's  going to pursue and look at everything  jamie did over this decade including  that are you all working with him at all  sharing your findings with him  um i mean we're we're the new york times  we're journalists so uh we're not  working with lawyers um  i mean could you potentially be  subpoenaed would you have to hand  anything  i don't know we'll see we haven't been  contacted yet by law enforcement  so from here  where do you to go i mean i think the  fans and ever the public were so  incredibly captivated to see a second  piece from you will there be more from  here  you know we're still continuing to  report the start of story is far from  over so we're still looking for people  with uh you know first-hand experience  and and evidence of anything they want  to come forward and tell us about  and we'll see what happens we filmed  here today just in case so  yeah i think there's definitely a lot  more to report over the last 13 years a  lot happened a lot of money was made a  lot of people were involved and we want  to investigate everything  being in the courtroom today if you can  just kind of you know give me your your  version your take on what the experience  was like the back and forth between  those lawyers so there was a really long  back and forth between britney's la